        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a bank without Qi2 certification</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A bank labeled only “MagSafe compatible” usually charges an iPhone at 7.5W or less, runs hotter and may hold weakly. Qi2 certification is the simplest filter for a bank that charges at 15W and lines up properly. Check for the Qi2 logo or certification in the listing, not just the word magnetic.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Using a non-magnetic case</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Magnetic banks attach through the case. A thick case without its own magnet ring weakens the hold, increases the gap between coils and slows charging while adding heat. If the bank keeps sliding off, the case is almost always the cause. A MagSafe-compatible case fixes it for the price of a few coffees.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting the rated mAh to reach the phone</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A 10,000mAh bank does not deliver 10,000mAh. Baseus itself says roughly 5,500 to 6,500mAh is usable after losses on its 10K bank. Plan on about one full charge of a standard phone from a 10K bank used wirelessly, and less for a large Pro Max model.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Charging wirelessly when a cable is available</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Wireless is the convenient way to charge and the wasteful one. When you are sitting down with a cable, use the USB-C port: it is faster, cooler and wastes less of the bank’s capacity. Save the magnetic pad for when you are walking, driving or need both hands.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Leaving the bank on a hot dashboard</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Heat ages lithium cells and makes iPhones throttle charging. A magnetic bank attached to a phone in a sunny car or on a dashboard is the worst case for both batteries. Keep the bank and phone shaded, and do not store a bank in a hot vehicle through summer.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
